FD_BUF[FD_LINE_END] = '\0';
```

`FD_LINE_TERMCHAR` is set to the character at `FD_BUF[FD_LINE_END]`, which is the character after the newline. This could be uninitialized if `FD_LINE_END` is at the end of the buffer (i.e., `FD_BUF_END`). But `FD_BUF[FD_BUF_END]` was set to '\0' by the previous call, so it's initialized.

